#: assets/js/admin.js:2375
#: assets/js/admin.js:2639
msgid "Basic Usage"
msgstr ""

#: assets/js/admin.js:2381
msgid "You can easily create a click-to-call button using the All-in-One WP Sticky Anything plugin. Just follow the steps below."
msgstr ""

#: assets/js/admin.js:2381
msgid "1. Log in to your WordPress dashboard."
msgstr ""

#: assets/js/admin.js:2381
msgid "2. From the left menu, go to Sticky Anything → Click to Call."
msgstr ""

#: assets/js/admin.js:2381
msgid "3. Turn on the \"Click to Call\" option."
msgstr ""

#: assets/js/admin.js:2381
msgid "4. Enter your phone number and adjust the settings as needed."
msgstr ""

#: assets/js/admin.js:2381
msgid "5. Click the \"Save Changes\" button."
msgstr ""

#: assets/js/admin.js:2381
msgid "6. Visit your website to see the click-to-call button in action."
msgstr ""

#: assets/js/admin.js:2387
msgid "You can easily create a fixed (sticky) widget using the All-in-One WP Sticky Anything plugin. Just follow the steps below."
msgstr ""

#: assets/js/admin.js:2387
msgid "1. Go to your WordPress Dashboard → Appearance → Widgets."
msgstr ""

#: assets/js/admin.js:2387
msgid "2. If you are using the Block Editor, wrap the widget inside a Group block, then enable the Fixed Widget option from the Group settings in the right sidebar."
msgstr ""

#: assets/js/admin.js:2387
msgid "3. If you are using the Classic Editor, simply enable the Fixed Widget option and click the Save button."
msgstr ""

#: assets/js/admin.js:2387
msgid "4. Your sidebar widget will now remain fixed while scrolling."
msgstr ""

#: assets/js/admin.js:2393
msgid "You can make Sticky Header easily by All-in-one WP Sticky Anyting. You need to do some step for it."
msgstr ""

#: assets/js/admin.js:2393
msgid "1. Go to WordPress Dashboard > Sticky Anything > Settings > General"
msgstr ""

#: assets/js/admin.js:2393
msgid "2. In the \"Sticky Class\" field, enter the CSS selector of your header. Must you need to provide a valid css class or id selector. example: .header"
msgstr ""

#: assets/js/admin.js:2393
msgid "3. If sticky header z-index issue on scroll, then you need to configure the \"Z-index\" field. Write the max big integer value. ex: 9999999"
msgstr ""

#: assets/js/admin.js:2393
msgid "4. Now you can click save button on the header."
msgstr ""

#: assets/js/admin.js:2399
msgid "You can create a Sticky Header in Elementor without extra plugins. Just follow these steps:"
msgstr ""

#: assets/js/admin.js:2399
msgid "1. Open any page with Elementor editor."
msgstr ""

#: assets/js/admin.js:2399
msgid "2. Select the container or section you want to make sticky."
msgstr ""

#: assets/js/admin.js:2399
msgid "3. Go to the \"Advanced\" tab in the Elementor panel."
msgstr ""

#: assets/js/admin.js:2399
msgid "4. Scroll down to the \"Sticky Anything\" section and enable the \"Sticky\" option."
msgstr ""

#: assets/js/admin.js:2399
#: assets/js/admin.js:2414
msgid "6. Adjust \"Z-index\" if needed to control the stacking order."
msgstr ""

#: assets/js/admin.js:2399
msgid "7. Update/Publish the page to apply the changes."
msgstr ""

#: assets/js/admin.js:2414
msgid "You can create a Sticky Header via Customizer without any hussle. Just follow these steps:"
msgstr ""

#: assets/js/admin.js:2414
msgid "1. Navigate Appearance > Customize."
msgstr ""

#: assets/js/admin.js:2414
msgid "2. Navigate to the \"Sticky Anything\" section."
msgstr ""

#: assets/js/admin.js:2414
msgid "3. Navigate to the \"Sticky Header\" section."
msgstr ""

#: assets/js/admin.js:2414
msgid "4. Enable the \"Sticky Header\" option."
msgstr ""

#: assets/js/admin.js:2414
msgid "7. Click the Publish bytton on the customizer."
msgstr ""

#: assets/js/admin.js:2429
#: assets/js/admin.js:2435
msgid "You can make Sticky Social Icons easily by All-in-one WP Sticky Anyting. You need to do some step for it."
msgstr ""

#: assets/js/admin.js:2429
msgid "1. Go to WordPress Dashboard → Sticky Anything → Settings → Social Icons."
msgstr ""

#: assets/js/admin.js:2429
msgid "2. Enable the \"Sticky Social Icons\" option."
msgstr ""

#: assets/js/admin.js:2429
msgid "3. Customize the social icons settings to your preference."
msgstr ""

#: assets/js/admin.js:2429
msgid "4. Click \"Add Icon\" to insert social icons, then configure the icon and URL."
msgstr ""

#: assets/js/admin.js:2429
#: assets/js/admin.js:2435
#: assets/js/admin.js:2441
msgid "5. Click the \"Save\" button at the top to apply your changes."
msgstr ""

#: assets/js/admin.js:2435
msgid "1. Go to WordPress Dashboard → Sticky Anything → Settings → Sticky Cookie Consent."
msgstr ""

#: assets/js/admin.js:2435
msgid "2. Enable the \"Sticky Cookie Consent\" option."
msgstr ""

#: assets/js/admin.js:2435
msgid "3. Customize the cookie consent message, button text & style."
msgstr ""

#: assets/js/admin.js:2441
#: assets/js/admin.js:2824
msgid "Display a sticky table of contents to help users navigate your content."
msgstr ""

#: assets/js/admin.js:2441
msgid "1. Go to WordPress Dashboard → Sticky Anything → Settings → Sticky Table of Contents."
msgstr ""

#: assets/js/admin.js:2441
msgid "2. Enable the \"Table of Contents\" option."
msgstr ""

#: assets/js/admin.js:2441
msgid "3. Enable the \"Sticky\" option."
msgstr ""

#: assets/js/admin.js:2441
msgid "4. Customize the table of contents settings to your preference."
msgstr ""

#: assets/js/admin.js:2447
msgid "You can make any sticky element or sidebar easily on your WordPress website by All-in-one WP Sticky Anyting. Integration is super easy. You need add a class on your target element. ex: sticky."
msgstr ""

#: assets/js/admin.js:2453
msgid "Setting up a sticky sidebar on your WordPress site is simple with the All-in-One WP Sticky Anything plugin. Just follow these steps to get started:"
msgstr ""

#: assets/js/admin.js:2453
msgid "1. Go to your WordPress Dashboard. Navigate to: Sticky Anything > Settings > Sticky Sidebar."
msgstr ""

#: assets/js/admin.js:2453
msgid "2. Enable the Sticky Sidebar. Toggle the option to enable the sticky sidebar functionality."
msgstr ""

#: assets/js/admin.js:2453
msgid "3. Enter the Sidebar Selector. This is the class or ID of the sidebar you want to make sticky. Since it varies depending on your theme, right-click on your sidebar in the browser and select Inspect. Copy the relevant selector name (e.g., .sidebar or #secondary) and paste it into the Sidebar Selector field."
msgstr ""

#: assets/js/admin.js:2453
msgid "4. Enter the Sidebar Container Selector. This is the outer container that holds the sidebar. Again, inspect the element in your browser and copy the correct selector. Paste it into the Sidebar Container Selector field."
msgstr ""

#: assets/js/admin.js:2453
msgid "5. Adjust additonal settings based on your needs."
msgstr ""

#: assets/js/admin.js:2453
msgid "6. Now you can click save button on the header."
msgstr ""

#: assets/js/admin.js:2459
msgid "If needed, add custom CSS to fine-tune the appearance and behavior of the sticky header. Your custom css need to paste on the Custom CSS box and Click Save button."
msgstr ""

